3,1,"Will this happen?"],["5195260b_6ae525d0",43,-3,0,"I would suggest to move these two methods to the coordinator. It would be more clear why the reverse order is needed. You can let the coordinator to get mLandscapeSize and mProtraitSize first, adn…"],["68124a4a_bbd2506a",43,-3,1,"Can we use BackgroundImageInfo to store the two Point and the two Matrix instances?"],["745b5a70_99e2c943",42,-3,1,"Nit: move the check of if (portraitMatrix == null) before step 2."],["74bfd9e5_8b346d80",44,-3,0,"Move the logic of getPortraitWindowDimensions and getLandscapeWindowDimensions in this class. See my previous comments."],["adc4bf51_fa9e9054",43,-3,0,"Can you add a comment explaining why we need the reversed dimensions here? Besides, suggest to add a helper function like: getWindowDimensionsImpl(Configuration configuration, boolean…"],["c464dc4e_35025c0f",42,-3,1,"Nit: make this as a helper method with variable Matrix and Point (windowSize)."],["fcd9f8b2_03a30f94",45,-3,1,"Nit: java doc for public methods."],["fd1604c0_4ba03994",43,-3,1,"Does this method need to be public? I would suggest to audit all methods of these classes in this CL to make sure the modifiers are set correctly. Add @VisibleForTesting where appropriate."],["528ba5eb_5e411346",42,0,1,"Nit: use StringBuilder to build the string."],["f424925c_f0f5d880",43,0,1,"You have check the windowSize != null, so we could remove it here."],["f62d9bc1_8a7cf2cb",42,0,1,"Log.i(). Usually we don't use Log.e in production code."]],0,73],[7225773,20430,201,4.195,3.394,[[0,44]],[["54431807_e7d60212",39,-3,1,"Let's make getDeepCopy() handles the null case."],["74ba2e50_197445f1",39,-3,1,"How about adding a method getMatrix(orientation) or getMatrix(boolean isPortrait)?"],["dd5d5abc_0b738dc4",39,-3,1,"ditto."],["e593da38_51d7b7e4",42,-3,1,"Add java doc for public methods or change the modifiers to package-private when appropriate."],["29b4e900_dc4faadd",45,0,1,"Revert."]],0,74],[7252512,20434,14,0.407,0.29,[[12,0.625,2,9],[9,0.3